{"name":"Opal","hex":"#aee0e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Opal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A unisex given name from English from the precious stone, invented in the nineteenth century.\nA female given name from English from the precious stone, invented in the nineteenth century.\n\n A male given name from English from the precious stone, invented in the nineteenth century.","A female given name from English from the precious stone, invented in the nineteenth century."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Opal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Opal","blocks":[{"text":"Opal is a hydrated amorphous form of silica (SiO2·nH2O); its water content may range from 3% to 21% by weight, but is usually between 6% and 10%. Due to the amorphous (chemical) physical structure, it is classified as a mineraloid, unlike crystalline forms of silica, which are considered minerals. It is deposited at a relatively low temperature and may occur in the fissures of almost any kind of rock, being most commonly found with limonite, sandstone, rhyolite, marl, and basalt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Opal-53714.jpg/330px-Opal-53714.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opal","wikidata":"Q171058"},{"title":"Opal (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Opal was an American rock band in the 1980s. They were part of the Paisley Underground musical style.\nThe band's name is derived from \"Opel\", a song by Syd Barrett."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f4/Opal_band_photo.jpg/330px-Opal_band_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opal_(band)","wikidata":"Q3882803"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Opal_molecular_structure2.jpg/500px-Opal_molecular_structure2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa